## Deployment Strategy

### Option A: Vercel (Recommended) ⭐
1. Push code to GitHub
2. Connect Vercel to repo (free tier)
3. Auto-deploys on push
4. Get URL like `ski-tracker.vercel.app`
5. Open on iPhone Safari → Add to Home Screen

### Option B: Netlify
1. Drag & drop folder to netlify.com
2. Instant deployment
3. Free HTTPS included

### Option C: Local Testing
1. Run `npx serve .` in project directory
2. Access via local network IP on iPhone
3. Full functionality for development

> [!TIP]
> **To install on your iPhone:**
> 1. Open the deployed URL in Safari
> 2. Tap the Share button (box with arrow)
> 3. Scroll down and tap "Add to Home Screen"
> 4. The app will now launch full-screen like a native app!

---

## Verification Plan

### Automated Testing
Since this is a PWA with hardware dependencies (GPS), most testing will be manual, but I'll verify:

```bash
# Run local server
cd /Users/sebastianfackelmann/Documents/Projects/SKI_APP
npx serve .
```

### Manual Verification (Browser Testing via Browser Tool)
1. **Map Rendering** - Verify Kitzbühel ski area displays correctly
2. **UI Responsiveness** - Test mobile layout at 375px width (iPhone)
3. **Dark Mode Styling** - Confirm premium visual appearance
4. **PWA Manifest** - Verify service worker registration

### Manual Verification (Requires User)
1. **GPS Tracking on iPhone**
   - Open app in Safari on iPhone
   - Grant location permission
   - Walk/move and verify speed updates
   - Verify altitude reading matches reality

2. **Install to Home Screen**
   - Safari → Share → Add to Home Screen
   - Launch app from home screen
   - Verify full-screen mode (no browser chrome)
   - Verify app works offline (airplane mode)

3. **Performance on Slope**
   - Test at actual ski speed (30-80 km/h)
   - Verify speed calculation accuracy
   - Test with gloves (touch targets size)

